      ],
      "print_plain": "System 3 opens with a brace and the reprinted clefs. No barline stands before the notes. This is the second part of the cadenza that began at x 988 on system 2, and it ends at the thin-thick double bar. The longest voice is the upper staff: an eighth rest (1/2), an eighth-note triplet (1), a dotted quarter (3/2), an eighth (1/2), two eighth-note triplets (2), and four eighths (2), ending at the thin stroke. Those durations sum to 15/2 quarters. A lower voice, a dotted half then a chord with a turn and a fermata, sounds under the first part of that line and is shorter. The lower staff is empty until the double bar. The thin stroke is at x 763 and the thick stroke at x 767-768, with no repeat dots."
